sequenceDiagram
    title Striply Login and Refresh-Token Lifecycle — Phase 1 v0.1

    actor User
    participant Browser as React browser client
    participant API as Spring Boot API
    participant Auth as Identity application service
    participant Password as Password hasher
    participant Tokens as Token service
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Note over User,DB: Scope: synchronous HTTPS login and refresh flows. Database writes shown inside transaction boundaries.

    rect rgb(235, 245, 255)
        Note over User,DB: Login
        User->>Browser: Submit email and password
        Browser->>API: POST /api/v1/auth/login (HTTPS, JSON)
        API->>Auth: Authenticate normalized email and password
        Auth->>DB: Load user by normalized email
        Auth->>Password: Verify against stored hash or fixed dummy hash
        Password-->>Auth: Verification result

        alt User exists and credentials are valid
            Auth->>Tokens: Generate 5-minute access token and random refresh token
            Auth->>DB: BEGIN transaction
            Auth->>DB: Insert token family with 30-day absolute expiry
            Auth->>DB: Insert hash of first refresh token with 7-day expiry
            Auth->>DB: COMMIT transaction
            Auth-->>API: Authentication result
            API-->>Browser: 200 + access token Set-Cookie refresh token
        else Unknown email, wrong password, or disabled user
            Auth-->>API: Generic authentication failure
            API-->>Browser: 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
        end
    end

    rect rgb(238, 250, 238)
        Note over User,DB: Successful refresh rotation
        Browser->>API: POST /api/v1/auth/refresh (HTTPS + HttpOnly cookie)
        API->>API: Validate request origin / CSRF protection
        API->>Auth: Refresh using presented secret
        Auth->>Tokens: Hash presented refresh token
        Auth->>DB: BEGIN transaction
        Auth->>DB: Lock and load token family by token hash

        alt Token is unconsumed and token/family lifetimes are valid
            Auth->>DB: Atomically set consumed_at on current token
            Auth->>Tokens: Generate replacement refresh token and access token
            Auth->>DB: Insert replacement hash in same family
            Auth->>DB: COMMIT transaction
            Auth-->>API: Rotated authentication result
            API-->>Browser: 200 + access token replace refresh cookie
        else Token or family is expired, revoked, malformed, or unknown
            Auth->>DB: ROLLBACK or finish without mutation
            Auth-->>API: Generic refresh failure
            API-->>Browser: 401 INVALID_REFRESH_TOKEN clear cookie
        else Token was already consumed
            Auth->>DB: Revoke affected token family with TOKEN_REUSE reason
            Auth->>DB: Record security event without token data
            Auth->>DB: COMMIT transaction
            Auth-->>API: Generic refresh failure
            API-->>Browser: 401 INVALID_REFRESH_TOKEN clear cookie
        end
    end

    rect rgb(255, 242, 235)
        Note over Browser,DB: Concurrent use of the same refresh token
        par Request A
            Browser->>API: Refresh with token A1
            API->>Auth: Rotate A1
            Auth->>DB: Atomically consume A1 and insert A2
            DB-->>Auth: Rotation succeeds
            Auth-->>API: Access token + raw A2
            API-->>Browser: 200 replace cookie with A2
        and Request B
            Browser->>API: Refresh with the same token A1
            API->>Auth: Rotate A1
            Auth->>DB: Attempt to consume A1 after serialization/lock wait
            DB-->>Auth: A1 is already consumed
            Auth->>DB: Revoke Family A as suspected replay
            Auth-->>API: Generic refresh failure
            API-->>Browser: 401 INVALID_REFRESH_TOKEN clear cookie
        end
        Note over Browser,DB: Strict policy: Family A is revoked, so A2 is unusable and the user must log in again.
    end
